# Python environment and caches -- environment-specific / regenerable
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Build intermediate for the HTML report (regenerated by quickfix_portfolio.py)
output/_equity_data.json

# The R-cut trade caches, one per stop anchor: several MB of engine output
# each, regenerable by rerunning build_1m_rcut_report.py. They exist so a new
# METRIC costs seconds instead of 96 minutes of backtesting -- worth keeping on
# disk, not worth versioning.
output/quickfix1m1dcRcut*_trades.json

# The %R/24hRange pane's series: one file per market of engine output that
# charter copies into its (already ignored) site/. Regenerated by every
# run_1m_matrix.py pass, so it would churn megabytes of generated data into
# a commit on every refresh. Same call as the R-cut cache above.
output/ratio/

# GENERATED OUTPUT: renderings and bulk research grids (Lode, 2026-08-18).
# output/ was tracked whole and it was 11.1 MB of an 11.8 MB repo, rewritten
# by every refresh, so a commit read as ~40,000 lines of regenerated JSON and
# the code changes were invisible inside it. The .git directory had reached
# 61 MB against ~0.7 MB of actual source. The test applied: does anyone ever
# need to READ this at a past commit? An HTML page is a view of the JSON
# beside it, and the R-cut grids' conclusions live in the audit, so no.
# What stays tracked is the measured RESULT and the things that are small:
# quickfix1m1dc_all.json (the blotter), charter_trades_*.json (the hand-off),
# quickfix1m1dc_levels.json, and published_history.jsonl, which is appended
# rather than rewritten and carries the history these files were pretending
# to keep. Regenerate any of the below with the Update button.
output/*.html
output/quickfix1m1dcRcut4th5th.json
output/quickfix1m1dcRcutHybrid.json
output/quickfix1m1dc_matrix.json
